Let \(k\) be a positive integer.
We say that \(\mathcal{B}\) is \emph{\(k\)-pre-complete} 
if \({\mathrm{preHang}}(v,\mathcal{B}) > k\)
for every \(v\) in \(V(G)\).

Let \(k\) and \(\ell\) be positive integers
	and let \(\mathcal{B}\) be a \(k\)-complete \(\ell\)-tracking decomposition of a graph \(G\).
	If \(\mathcal{B}\) contains a full-augmenting sequence, 
	then there is an \(\ell\)-tracking decomposition \(\mathcal{B}'\) of \(G\) 
	such that the following holds.
	\begin{itemize}
	 \item \(\tau(\mathcal{B}') < \tau(\mathcal{B})\);
	 \item \(\mathcal{B}'(v) = \mathcal{B}(v)\) for every $v\in V(G)$;
	 \item $\mathcal{B}'$ is \(k\)-complete.
	\end{itemize}

