Let \(\ell\) be a positive integer and let \(G\) be a graph.
	If $\mathcal{B}$ is a feasible \(k\)-complete \(\ell\)-tracking decomposition of $G$
	and \(\tau(\mathcal{B}) > 0\),
	then there is an \(\ell\)-tracking decomposition \(\mathcal{B}'\) of \(G\) 
	such that the following holds.
	\begin{itemize}
	 \item \(\tau(\mathcal{B}') < \tau(\mathcal{B})\);
	 \item \(\mathcal{B}'(v) = \mathcal{B}(v)\) for every $v\in V(G)$;
	 \item $\mathcal{B}'$ is \(k\)-complete.
	\end{itemize}

Let \(k\) and \(\ell\) be positive integers such that $k-\ell$ is a 
positive even number. Let $G=(V,E)$ be a graph and let \(X\subset V\).
We say that a partition \(\mathcal{F}=\{M_1,\ldots,M_\ell,F_1,\ldots,F_{(k-\ell)/2}\}\) of $E$ is an 
\emph{\((X,\ell,k)\)-fractional factorization} of $G$ if the following holds.
	\begin{itemize}
		\item \(M_i\) is an \((X,1,k)\)-factor of $G$, for $1\leq i\leq \ell$;
		\item \(F_j\) is an Eulerian \((X,2,k)\)-factor of $G$, for $1\leq j\leq (k-\ell)/2$.	
	\end{itemize}

